4. Full-gate PTY findings and corrections

The first exact make test exited 2 (underlying cargo test 101) at the physical
PTY-master-close orphan assertion. make-test-initial.log and test-initial.json
preserve the failure. The final fixes keep every case and its 250ms/2s guards:

- tests/support/seat_shutdown.rs uses a descriptor-only writer. portable-pty's
  normal writer Drop injects newline+VEOF, which previously sent graceful
  Ctrl-D before the intended physical master close. writer_drop_is_not_cooked_eof
  observes the real slave read and rejects injected input.
- headless.rs requests POLLIN when polling for HUP. A native PTY witness reads
  cooked Ctrl-D as EOF without HUP, then closes the master and requires HUP.
  On Darwin the old events=0 poll missed HUP while termios still succeeded.
  The next full gate exposed an immediate-classification race in this new unit
  witness (exit2/cargo101). make-test-pty-unit-failure.log and its JSON retain it.
  The final witness first observes real physical EOF under a kernel hang guard,
  then classifies it. This changes only the test precondition; the production
  POLLIN fix is unchanged. pty-poll-final contains the refreshed 101 -> 0.
- tests/seat_process.rs closes unrelated descriptors in the non-PTY key child,
  matching portable-pty's pre-exec fence. A captured failing run showed sibling
  key process 40779 still holding master major15/minor25, fd6, while seat40783
  had slave major16/minor25. Thus the supposed final master close was not EOF.
  pty-failure-extract.log keeps only the relevant own-fixture records.
  non_pty_spawn_does_not_keep_a_sibling_master_alive explicitly clears CLOEXEC
  to force this window, observes an executed child through a byte handshake,
  then requires slave HUP. Its negative control retains the master in sleep.
  A first immediate poll in this new witness raced concurrent pre-exec cleanup;
  pty-isolation-first.* retain that failure. The final bounded poll is a kernel
  close hang guard, not a percentile benchmark or a relaxed product deadline.
- The Ctrl-D-at-the-prompt case now observes the rendered prompt before sending
  Ctrl-D. pty-before-prompt-barrier.* preserve the earlier exit-hang-guard failure.
  The close budget remains two seconds. No extra product watcher or polling
  thread was retained from the diagnostic experiments.

